## useEquipmentDeltas.ts
@flow-hash: 4012d14b

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Terminal
    participant useEquipmentDeltas
    participant EventDispatcher
    participant EquipmentStore
    participant EquipmentProfile
    participant EqDeltaParser
    participant TerminalTextExtractor

    User->>Terminal: Sends raw terminal data
    Terminal->>useEquipmentDeltas: Receives 'shatteredarchive:raw-data' event
    useEquipmentDeltas->>TerminalTextExtractor: Extracts text from terminal chunk
    TerminalTextExtractor-->>useEquipmentDeltas: Extracted text lines
    useEquipmentDeltas->>EqDeltaParser: Parses each line for equipment deltas
    EqDeltaParser-->>useEquipmentDeltas: Parsed delta events
    useEquipmentDeltas->>EquipmentStore: Reads current equipment state
    useEquipmentDeltas->>EquipmentProfile: Gets snapshot data
    alt Event Type
        useEquipmentDeltas->>EquipmentStore: Updates equipment state (wield, wear, etc.)
        useEquipmentDeltas->>EquipmentStore: Patches snapshot data
        useEquipmentDeltas->>EventDispatcher: Dispatches relevant events (wield, wear, remove, etc.)
    end
    EventDispatcher-->>User: Notifies UI of equipment changes
```

Caption: The hook listens for terminal updates, parses equipment deltas, and synchronizes state and snapshots while dispatching UI events.

## useGameConnection.ts
@flow-hash: e26904b9

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant H as React Hook (useGameConnection)
    participant E as EventEmitter
    participant W as WebSocket
    participant S as Game Server
    participant D as DSL Processor
    participant T as Terminal Writer

    H->>W: Creates WebSocket connection
    W->>S: Connects via ws:// or wss://
    S->>W: Sends 'connect' message
    W->>H: Triggers 'open' event
    H->>E: Dispatches 'game:remote-server:open'

    H->>W: Sends 'data' message
    W->>S: Forwards data
    S->>W: Sends 'raw' or 'gmcp' message
    W->>H: Triggers 'message' event
    H->>E: Dispatches 'game:remote-server:raw' or 'game:remote-server:gmcp'

    H->>E: Listens for 'shatteredarchive:send-command'
    E->>D: Processes DSL to ANSI
    D->>T: Writes to terminal
    H->>W: Sends command via WebSocket

    H->>W: Calls disconnect()
    W->>S: Closes connection
    W->>H: Triggers 'close' event
    H->>E: Dispatches 'game:remote-server:close'
```

Caption: The React hook manages a WebSocket connection to a game server, handling data flow between the client, server, and UI components via event emitters and terminal rendering.

## useMainContainer.ts
@flow-hash: ccb13052

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant ReactComponent
    participant useMainContainer
    participant localStorage
    participant initBrowserLuaRunner
    participant ensureAudioRuntimeAttached
    participant getAccessibilitySettings
    participant buildAccessibilityCss
    participant ensureStyleTag
    participant applyUserCss
    participant applyCombinedCss

    ReactComponent->>useMainContainer: Hook called
    useMainContainer->>localStorage: Read rightPaneWidth
    useMainContainer->>localStorage: Read bottomPaneHeight
    useMainContainer->>initBrowserLuaRunner: Initialize Lua runtime
    useMainContainer->>ensureAudioRuntimeAttached: Attach audio runtime
    useMainContainer->>getAccessibilitySettings: Get accessibility settings
    useMainContainer->>buildAccessibilityCss: Build accessibility CSS
    useMainContainer->>ensureStyleTag: Ensure style tag exists
    useMainContainer->>applyUserCss: Apply user CSS
    useMainContainer->>applyCombinedCss: Combine and apply all CSS
    localStorage->>useMainContainer: Return layout values
    ReactComponent->>useMainContainer: Return layout vars and handlers
    ReactComponent->>useMainContainer: Return menu state handlers
    ReactComponent->>useMainContainer: Return CSS override handlers
    useMainContainer->>localStorage: Save layout changes
    useMainContainer->>localStorage: Save user CSS
    ReactComponent->>useMainContainer: Return modal open/close handlers
```

Caption: The main container hook orchestrates layout sizing, menu state, user CSS overrides, and modal management while interacting with browser storage and external runtime initialization.

## useUserScriptSandbox.ts
@flow-hash: 30b5a2bf

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant H as Human (UI)
    participant R as React Hook (useUserScriptSandbox)
    participant LS as localStorage
    participant RS as RuntimeSingleton
    participant GE as GameEmitter
    participant GS as GlobalScriptsStore
    participant UV as UserVariablesStore
    participant API as External API (fetch)

    H->>R: Load scripts
    R->>LS: Get scripts from localStorage
    LS-->>R: Return scripts or empty array
    R->>R: Set scripts state

    H->>R: Create/Update/Delete script
    R->>R: Update scripts state
    R->>LS: Save scripts to localStorage
    LS-->>R: Confirm save

    R->>GE: Listen for socket events
    GE-->>R: socket open/close

    H->>R: Run script
    R->>R: Make API base
    R->>RS: Run script via RuntimeSingleton
    RS->>GS: Access global vars
    GS-->>RS: Return global var value
    RS->>UV: Get user variables
    UV-->>RS: Return snapshot
    RS->>API: Make HTTP request
    API-->>RS: Return response
    RS->>R: Return result

    R->>GE: Dispatch events (send-command, write-terminal)
    GE-->>H: UI updates
```

Caption: The human interacts with the user script sandbox through UI actions, which triggers React hooks to manage scripts, persist them to localStorage, and execute them via RuntimeSingleton, with interaction
